{{define "title"}}Sign in{{end}}
{{define "main"}}
<main class="gate">
  <div class="panel stack">
    <h1>Sign in to read git repositories</h1>
    <p class="meta">Branches and tags, the commit log, what a commit changed, and any file.</p>
    {{- if .Refused}}
    <p class="notice"><strong>You are signed out.</strong> The installation did not accept the credential this session held. Sign in again to carry on.</p>
    {{- end}}
    <p><a class="button button-primary" href="/auth/start?return_to={{.ReturnTo}}">{{.ButtonLabel}}</a></p>
    <p class="meta prose">There is no password and no sign-up here. Access follows the account your organisation already gave you, and what you may read is decided by the installation, not by this page.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="panel stack">
    <h2>Clone address</h2>
    <p class="clone-shape">{{.CloneHTTPS}}{{if .CloneSSH}}
{{.CloneSSH}}{{end}}</p>
    <p class="meta prose">Cloning needs the same account. Replace the two names with the repository you want.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="panel stack">
    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p class="meta prose">This is {{if .Hosted}}a hosted installation of {{end}}{{.View.ProjectName}}, an open-source git server. Anyone can read the code, and anyone can run their own.</p>
    <p><a href="{{.View.ProjectURL}}">The {{.View.ProjectName}} project</a></p>
  </div>
</main>
{{end}}
